{"_data": [{"contents": [{"content": "Presenting the Product", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Cultural Sensitivity", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 2, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 14, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Explain customs and appropriate behaviour at work and in different countries, using a wider range of expressions and formulas. ", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Understands important and specific information and aspects of attitude and intention in conversations, texts or presentations about the communicative functions related to this level.", "type": "secondary_8"}], "type": "objectives"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Passive of Modal Verbs", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " The passive voice is commonly used in English. We use the passive when the 'doer' (agent) of the action it not so important. We are not interested in knowing who did the action. Our attention is on the object. Here's some more information about the passive of modal verbs. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "a. Future form: subject + will + be + past participle<span class=\"italic\"><ul> <li>This issue <span class=\"underline\">will be dealt</span>  with.</li> <li>A new spokesperson <span class=\"underline\">will be identified</span> . </li> <li>Updated plans and new developments on the story <span class=\"underline\">will be sent</span>  as early and as often as possible. </li> </span> </ul>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "b. Modals: can / could + be + past participle <br/> We use these forms to talk about present and past possibility. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>No one <span class=\"underline\">can be prepared</span>  for a crisis like this. </li> <li>This <span class=\"underline\">could be done</span>  with a simple e-mail.</li> </ul></span> ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "c. Modals: must / should + be + past participle<br/> These forms are used to talk about necessity and advisability. <span class=\"italic\"><ul><li>The spokesperson <span class=\"underline\">should be prepared</span>  to deal with the media and partake in interviews.</li> <li>It <span class=\"underline\">should be emphasized</span>  that we will continue to operate as usual.</li> <li>Current updates <span class=\"underline\">should be reflected</span>  in our plan. </li> <li>Media updates <span class=\"underline\">must be given</span>  to ensure we cover our bases. </li> <li>Transparency <span class=\"underline\">must be projected</span>  in our speech. </li> </span> ", "type": "text"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": " Be Supposed To", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " In the business world, expectations are common since there are rules, agreements or people who are in charge. When we talk about those expectations, we use the expression \u201cbe supposed to\u201d. Here's more on how you can use it. ", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "a. Form: be + (not) + supposed to + bare infinitive (verb without to)", "type": "text"}, {"content": "b. Meaning: \u201cBe supposed to\u201d shows expectations. Someone expects you to do something in the present or in the future. It can also describe a past expectation. ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "We know this <span class=\"underline\">wasn't supposed to</span>  happen. (It happened but we didn't expect it to happen)", "type": "example"}, {"content": "<span class=\"underline\">Are</span>  we <span class=\"underline\">supposed to</span>  inform the company's employees? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We'<span class=\"underline\">re supposed to</span>  communicate with people. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I <span class=\"underline\">am supposed to</span> hear back from them by next week. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "A<span class=\"underline\">m I supposed to</span>  be at the meeting on Tuesday? ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "He'<span class=\"underline\">s supposed to</span>  help me with that.", "type": "example"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"content": "spokesperson ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "someone who speaks to the public on behalf of an organization", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: A spokesperson will make the statement. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob02aud01", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " These are words you use to deal with a crisis.", "type": "text"}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to ensure", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to make certain that something happens", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Media attraction must be given to ensure we cover all the media sources.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob02aud02", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to concur", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to agree", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: I concur with your assessment.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob02aud03", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "a lack of", "type": "name"}, {"content": "not enough of something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Also, nothing generates more media coverage than a lack of honesty. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob02aud04", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "transparency", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a business activity which is done openly and without secrets", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Consequently, transparency in our statements must be projected through all communication channels. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob02aud05", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": " to project ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to calculate an amount expected in the future", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Consequently, transparency in our statements must be projected through all communication channels. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob02aud06", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "to (not) say a word ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to keep a secret; to not speak about something", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Farmani mentioned not saying a word to customers and stakeholders.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob02aud07", "type": "audio"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Using point form, make a list of all the things that you need to do this week.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Convert each item on this list into a complete sentence using \u201cI am supposed to \u2026\u201d", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Share your list with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Provide your partner with feedback on how they might complete their tasks.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"content": "I make a \u201cto-do\u201d list.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I write about things I am supposed to do.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I share my plans with a partner.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "I provide my partner with feedback.", "type": "text"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}, {"content": "engenn8le14ob02re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}], "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "contents": [{}], "_data": [], "id": 0, "type": "welcome"}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"image": "engenn8le14ob02re2img05.jpg", "time": "0", "id": 0, "text": ""}, {"image": "engenn8le14ob02re2img06.jpg", "time": "200", "id": 1, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: My professor had always told me that 'one can never be prepared for a crisis'. He was right.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: We all know this wasn't supposed to happen, Janet. Let's focus. The issue will be dealt with. Where do we start?\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: I am supposed to hear back from Rocco by noon. A spokesperson  will be identified. Media attraction must be given to ensure we cover all the media sources.<br/>\n<span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: I concur. I've already contacted TV channels, radios and a few online bloggers. Our spokesperson should be prepared to answer media questions and participate in interviews."}, {"image": "engenn8le14ob02re2img07.jpg", "time": "36000", "id": 2, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Absolutely. Also, nothing generates more media coverage than a lack of  honesty. Consequently, transparency in our statements must be projected  through all communication channels.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: Are we supposed to inform Holly's employees?\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Yes. This could be done with a simple e-mail. It should be emphasized that business continues as smoothly as possible.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: Farmani mentioned not saying a word to customers and stakeholders."}, {"image": "engenn8le14ob02re2img06.jpg", "time": "66000", "id": 3, "text": "<span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: We are a personal relations firm, Miranda. We're supposed to communicate with people. We don't want them to learn about the crisis through the media. Notice must be given to them. Customers and stakeholders will be updated regularly as part of our crisis communication plan.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Miranda</span>: Right. Summary statements, updated action plans and new developments will be sent as early and as often as possible. Peter's supposed to help me with that.\n<br/> <span class=\"strong\">Janet</span>: Great. This plan might be given priority. We live in a time of 24/7 news cycles. This should be reflected in our crisis plan."}], "audiosrc": "engenn8le14ob02re2aud01", "coverimg": "engenn8le14ob02re2img05.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "id": 1}], "exercises": [{"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " I can explain basic rules, policies, or laws that could affect me negatively and answer questions about them.", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can talk about things I am supposed to do and things that are supposed to happen. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " I can discuss how to deal with problems. ", "type": "Learning Outcomes"}, {"content": " What was the most difficult thing you had to deal with at work?", "type": "Free Header Item"}, {"content": " How did you deal with it?", "type": "Free Header Item"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Welcome", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "You have 2 tries", "type": "text"}, {"content": "you have 1 attempt left", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "try again", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"content": " Ask your partner:", "type": "free_header_text"}, {"content": " The struggle is real.", "type": "free_type_text_area"}], "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "id": 0, "img_path": "", "stimuli_ids": [0]}, {"template_override": 1, "_data": [{"contents": [{"content": " \nThe team tries to <span class=\"tool-tip\" id=\"tip_1_0\">avert</span> the crisis.\n", "type": "text"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Content", "type": "group_name"}], "type": "group"}, {"content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"content": "", "type": "text"}, {"content": "", "type": "text"}], "incorrect_feedback": [{"content": "Whoops! Something important is missing.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Maybe next time...", "type": "text"}], "correct_feedback": "Correct!", "allowed_attempts": 2}, "type": "feedback"}, {"contents": [{"content": "Reading", "type": "skill"}, {"content": "Listening", "type": "skill"}], "type": "learning_skills"}, {"content": [{"content": " To <span class=\"italic\